description:
FILED s532c (Opus agent, 2026-11-08) while accepting #4502 on io/pipe.t: with the runaway children gone (#4502), the main process's own row 25 is measured for the first time, and it fails because of row 17's mechanism.
PROBE (scratch/s532c/p/4502-5.pl; perl 5.40.3):
  my $zombie; unless ($zombie = fork) { exit 37 }
  open *FH, "sleep 2;exit 13|" or die;
  $SIG{ALRM} = sub { return }; alarm(1);
  my $c = close FH;  print "close=[$c] status=", $? >> 8, "\n";      # perl: close=[] status=13     PCL: close=[] status=0
  my $wait = wait;   print "wait=", ($wait == $zombie ? "zombie" : $wait), "\n";   # both: zombie
  $? = 0; open NIL, '/no_such_process |'; close NIL;
  my $child = 0; eval { local $SIG{ALRM} = sub { die }; alarm 3; $child = wait; alarm 0 };
  print "child=", ($child == -1 ? -1 : "a pid"), "\n";               # perl: -1     PCL: a pid (the `sleep 2; exit 13` shell, $? >> 8 = 13)
MECHANISM (to confirm): %p-close-maybe-pipe's waitpid on the pipe child returns EINTR when SIGALRM arrives and the handler returns; perl's my_pclose loops on EINTR (PERL_ASYNC_CHECK, then waitpid again) until the child is reaped.  PCL gives up, answers close false with $? 0, and the child stays a zombie of the program.
FIX SHAPE: retry the waitpid on EINTR in the pipe-close path (after running the deferred signal handler), as perl does; a handler that DIES still propagates.  Guard: the probe above.
BOARD/COMPANION: io/pipe.t row 25 (NEW in the s532c acceptance run, keyed here) and row 17 'status' (blessed under the #1710 bundle) are this mechanism.
